// The booth's authored phrase banks (see BoothBanks.h): the wordings, as data. Included once, by Booth.cpp (an .inl, so
// the build scripts that list the booth's sources need nothing new, and the game's module does not compile it twice). Each table is one situation; a wording
// names the sim facts it needs in braces. New wordings go at the END of a bank (a wording's index is what the memory
// across games keeps). Facts most banks can use (Booth::facts): {off} {def} the offense's and defense's cities, {offn}
// {defn} their nicknames, {pf} {cf} the two men's first names, {dd} the down and distance now, {ddb} the one the play
// was run on, {qn} the quarter, {clock}, {seg} what the clock counts down to (quarter, half, game), {sc} the score
// ("Austin 14, Fresno 7" / "tied at 7" / "still scoreless"), {leader} {trailer} {hi} {lo} {margin} (empty when tied),
// {tied}, {sit} the offense's situation ("up 7", "down 3", "in a tie game"). The rest are the caller's.
//
// A tail that opens with ", " joins the line before it; one that opens with " " is its own sentence (Booth's bJoin).
